hadiths[97]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in residence and on journey. In residence, when he performed the Zuhr prayer, he would pray four rak‘ahs (obligatory) and then two rak‘ahs after them. And when he performed the Asr prayer, he would pray (only) four rak‘ahs (obligatory) and would not pray anything after them. And when he performed the Maghrib prayer, he would pray three rak‘ahs (obligatory) and then two rak‘ahs after them. And when he performed the ‘Isha prayer, he would perform four rak‘ahs (obligatory) and then two rak‘ahs after them. And I accompanied him on journey, so when he performed the Zuhr prayer, he would pray two rak‘ahs (obligatory) and then (also) two rak‘ahs after them. And when he performed the Asr prayer, he would pray (only) two rak‘ahs and would not pray anything after them. And when he performed the Maghrib prayer, he would pray three rak‘ahs (obligatory) and then two rak‘ahs after them. And he said: “This (Maghrib prayer) is the witr of the day with which the day ends and the night begins.” And when he performed the ‘Isha prayer, he would pray two rak‘ahs and then (also) two rak‘ahs after them."
"2","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, about a person in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) who wishes to sleep, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""He should perform ablution (wudu) like the ablution for prayer (and then sleep)."" And Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, whenever he wished to eat in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform ablution."
"3","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I performed prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in both residence and travel, so I performed with him in residence four rak‘ahs (obligatory) of Zuhr prayer and after it two rak‘ahs, and four rak‘ahs (obligatory) of Asr prayer and after it nothing, and three rak‘ahs (obligatory) of Maghrib prayer and after them two rak‘ahs, and four rak‘ahs (obligatory) of Isha prayer and after it two rak‘ahs. And I performed with him in travel two rak‘ahs (obligatory) of Zuhr prayer and after it two rak‘ahs, and (only) two rak‘ahs of Asr prayer and after them nothing, and three rak‘ahs (obligatory) of Maghrib prayer and after it two rak‘ahs (obligatory), and this prayer is the witr (odd) prayer of the day. There is no reduction in it in travel or residence, and two rak‘ahs (obligatory) of Isha prayer and after it two rak‘ahs were performed."
"4","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for hunting, or for herding animals, or a dog for frightening the enemy, then every day two qirats are reduced from his (good) deeds."" (Abdullah bin Umar was) asked, Abu Abdur Rahman! We hear of one qirat, so he replied: By Him besides whom there is no one worthy of worship, my ears heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying two qirats. Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman, Ibn Abi Layla says: I mentioned this to Nafi’ (may Allah have mercy on him), so he said: I heard Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrating this hadith, but I did not hear the words ""dog for frightening (the enemy)"" from him."
"5","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: A man asked the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, about the night prayer. So the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is (offered) two by two rak‘ahs, and if one fears the approach of morning (dawn), then let him pray one rak‘ah."""
"6","It is narrated from Ubaid bin Juraij, he said: Ubaid came to my father and said: I went to Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) and asked him about some matters, so he said: Speak, you always come to me for some purpose. I asked: I have not seen you touching any other corner except the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) doing this. Ibn Juraij said: I have only seen you wearing Sabti shoes. Asim said: By Sabti shoes is meant the shoe which, after the leather is cleaned and dyed and has no hair, is prepared. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) doing this (wearing Sabti shoes). He would perform ablution in them, pray in them, and he liked them."
"7","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, stood among us and said: ""Do not sell the fruit until its goodness (ripeness) becomes apparent."""
"8","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): (He was asked) Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibit making nabidh in clay pots and gourd vessels? He said: Yes."
"9","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I was sitting with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when a young man came to him and said: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! May I come closer to you? So he (the Prophet) said: ""Come closer."" He (the young man) came so close that he placed his thigh upon the Prophet’s thigh and said: O Messenger of Allah! What is Islam? He (the Prophet) said: You bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, He is alone, He has no partner, and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His Messenger. The young man asked: If I do this, am I a Muslim? He (the Prophet) said: ""Yes (you are a Muslim)."" He asked: What is faith (iman)? So he (the Prophet) said: ""You believe in good and bad destiny, you believe in Paradise and Hell, you believe in resurrection after death, and you believe in the (truth of the) scale (mizan)."" He (the young man) said: If I do this, am I a believer? He (the Prophet) said: Yes."
"10","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to teach us the Tashahhud in prayer just as a writing teacher teaches children."
"11","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Perform ablution after eating camel meat, and do not perform ablution after eating goat meat. Perform ablution after drinking she-camel's milk, and do not perform ablution after drinking goat's milk. Pray in sheep enclosures, and do not pray in camel enclosures."""
"12","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, those who dwell in the heavens do not hear anything from the people of the earth except the call to prayer (adhan)."""
"13","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: On the Day of Resurrection, the callers to prayer (muezzins) will have the longest necks among the people, and they will be the first to be clothed."
"14","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Of all the lawful things, the most disliked by Allah is divorce."""
"15","Abu Umayyah narrated to us, he said: Kathir bin Ubaid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Mukhlad narrated to us from Ma'rif bin Wasel, from Muharib bin Dithar, from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), and he narrated from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"16","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah has named them 'Abrar' (the righteous) because they did good to their parents and their children. Just as your parents have a right over you, so too your children have a right over you."""
"17","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, continuously enjoined (care of) prayer and slaves until his blessed tongue became silent."
"18","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he was asked: You exert (great) effort at the two corners, while we have not seen anyone else doing as you do. He replied: If I do so, it is because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Indeed, touching them erases sins."""
"19","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, tale-bearing is falsehood, and malice and (tribal and ignorant) zealotry are in the Hellfire. These two things cannot be combined in the heart of a Muslim."""
"20","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the woman who wails, the one who listens to wailing, the one who shaves her head (in mourning), the one who screams and wails, the one who tattoos, and the one who gets tattooed, and said: There is no reward for women in following funeral processions."
"21","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying, ""Tale-bearing, abusive language, and (ignorant) zealotry will lead to Hell, and these two things cannot be combined in the heart of a believer."""
"22","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: There was a time upon us when everyone considered his Muslim brother more deserving of dinar and dirham than himself, and today dinar and dirham are more beloved to us than our Muslim brothers. And this is because I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: ""When people become stingy with dinar and dirham, and follow the tails of cattle, and abandon striving in the way of Allah, and deceive in transactions, then Allah Almighty will impose disgrace upon them, and that disgrace will not be removed from them until they return to their religion."""
"23","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that whenever the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, would wake up at night, he would use the miswak."
"24","And the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “This Ummah of mine is the completion of seventy nations. We are the last of them and better than all of them.”"
"25","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever gives the adhan, he has the right to give the iqamah."
"26","Safwan bin Mahraz says: Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was performing Tawaf of the House of Allah when a man met him and said: O Abu Abdur Rahman! What have you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) regarding the manner of private conversation (with Allah)? He replied: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the believer will be brought close to his Lord, as if he is a lamb or a kid, and He will cover him and ask him: Do you know? Do you know? And he will say: O my Lord! I know, O my Lord! I know. He will ask again: Do you know? He will say: O my Lord! I know. He will ask again: Do you know? He will say: O my Lord! I know. Then Allah, the Exalted, will say: I concealed it for you in the world, and today I forgive you for it. Then he will be given the record of his good deeds."" And as for the disbelievers and hypocrites, a call will be made before all the people: These are the ones who lied against their Lord; beware, the curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers. Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him) said: On that day, no one will be disgraced who concealed his disgrace from the creation."
"27","Abdullah bin Ashtar says: By Allah! I was with Abdullah bin Muti’ when he, along with Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), attacked Yazid bin Muawiyah. At that time, Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) came to them. He asked for a cushion, which was presented to him, but he said: I have not come to sit with you, rather I intended to narrate to you a hadith which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever abandons obedience (to the ruler) will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection without having any proof (for his salvation), and whoever dies without having pledged allegiance (to a ruler) dies the death of ignorance.” Then (Abdullah bin Umar) returned."
"28","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, mentioned tribulation, and a man with his face covered passed by there. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said (regarding him): ""This oppressed one will be killed."" I looked at him, and he was Uthman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him."
"29","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Do not reside among the Nabatean tribes in their cities. And if they dispute with you in conversation, then avoid them. Beware of them, beware of them, and do not marry the people of Khuzestan, for there is treachery in their roots."
"30","Yasar bin Numair, the freed slave of Ibn Umar, says: Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saw me praying after the Fajr prayer and asked: O Yasar! How many rak‘ahs did you pray? I replied: I do not know. He said: You do not even know. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us while we were praying this prayer. He expressed displeasure with us and said: “Let those of you who are present convey to those who are absent. Indeed, after the rising of Fajr, there is no (nafl) prayer except for the two rak‘ahs (Sunnah of Fajr).”"
"31","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, without fasting on Friday."
"32","Ja'far says: I was sitting with Abdullah bin Umar and Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with them) when one of them said to the other: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the children of Adam will sweat."" One of them said: up to the earlobes, and the other said: it will reach up to the mouth like a bridle."
"33","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), a Bedouin asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): Which animals can a person in Ihram kill? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""He may kill the crow, the kite, the mouse, the biting dog, and the scorpion."" Ayyub says: I asked Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) about snakes, so he said: There is no difference of opinion regarding killing them."
"34","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever sells a date-palm tree after it has been pollinated, then its (current year's) fruit belongs to the seller, except if the buyer stipulates a condition."""
"35","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, cut off the hand (of a thief) because of the theft of a shield whose value was three dirhams."
"36","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of Muzabana, which is that a person sells the produce of his land for a known weight on the condition that if the produce turns out to be more, he will not get anything extra, and if the produce is less than the weight, he will be responsible for the loss. Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted the sale of dates on the tree (in exchange for an estimated amount of dry or fresh dates)."
"37","It is narrated from Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saw a dream in which it was as if there was a piece of silk in his hand, and wherever in Paradise he wished to go, it would carry him there flying. He related this dream to Umm al-Mu’minin, Lady Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her), and Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) related it to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Abdullah is a righteous man."""
"38","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When a slave worships his Lord well and obeys his master, he is given a double reward."
"39","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: I have never abandoned touching the Black Stone in any condition since I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, touching it."
"40","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you goes for Jumu'ah (Friday prayer), he should perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"41","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever intentionally kills a believer has certainly disbelieved in Allah."""
"42","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicating thing is khamr (wine)."""
"43","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he stated: We assumed the Ihram for Hajj Mufrad along with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."
"44","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person may be one who performs prayer, gives zakat, performs Hajj and Umrah, fasts, and engages in jihad, until he mentioned many acts of goodness, and on the Day of Resurrection he will receive reward and recompense according to his intention."""
"45","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is obligatory upon a Muslim to listen to and obey (the ruler's) command, whether he likes it or dislikes it."""
"46","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Offer the Witr prayer before dawn."""
"47","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), a man asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""What clothing can a person in Ihram wear?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""A person in Ihram should not wear a shirt, turban, trousers, cap, or leather socks. If shoes are not available, then he may wear leather socks, but he should cut them below the ankles. And he should not wear any garment that has been touched by wars or saffron (fragrance)."" Ibn Aun did not mention the turban."
"48","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he stated: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded us to kill the dogs around Madinah. We found ourselves even killing the dog of a woman coming from the villages."
"49","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should milk someone else's animal without the owner's permission. Does any one of you like that his treasury be broken into and everything taken from it? Indeed, the udders of animals are the treasuries of their owners."""
"50","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person in the state of Ihram should neither marry (himself) nor arrange the marriage (of someone else)."""
"51","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""For twenty-four camels, the zakat is five goats, until they become twenty-five. When they reach twenty-five, then among them is one 'bint makhad' (a one-year-old she-camel). If there is no 'bint makhad', then up to thirty-five, it is 'ibn labun' (a two-year-old male camel). Then, regarding the age of the zakat camels, the same situation is described as others narrate, until the number of camels reaches one hundred and twenty. When the number exceeds one hundred and twenty, then for every forty-five, one 'ibn labun', and for every sixty, one 'hiqqah' (a three-year-old she-camel) is due as zakat."""
"52","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: For every forty goats up to one hundred and twenty, one goat is due as zakat. When the number increases, then up to two hundred, two goats are due. When the number increases further, then up to three hundred, three goats are due. When the number increases beyond that, then for every hundred, one goat is due as zakat. (Out of fear of zakat) do not separate a combined herd, nor combine separate herds, and every two partners should settle accounts with each other equally, and the zakat collector should not be given an old, male, or defective animal, unless the one giving zakat wishes so."
"53","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he reported from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, similar to the previous hadith."
"54","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicating substance is wine, and every intoxicating substance is forbidden."""
"55","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked about fasting on the day of Ashura, so he said: The people of the pre-Islamic era used to venerate this day."
"56","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not proper for a Muslim who has something to bequeath, that he should spend two nights without having his will written and kept with him."""
"57","Nafi’ (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), when he was on a journey on a cold or rainy night and gave the call to prayer for ‘Isha, would say: “Pray in your dwellings.” Indeed, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) do the same on a cold and rainy night."
"58","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience (to the ruler) will meet Allah in such a state that he will have no proof for himself, and whoever dies in such a state that there is no pledge of allegiance on his neck, he dies the death of ignorance."""
"59","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, stoned a Jewish man and woman."
"60","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to combine Maghrib and Isha prayers while traveling when he was riding, and Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) states that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) needed to hasten in any matter, he would combine these two prayers."
"61","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever misses the Asr prayer until it is lost, it is as if his family and his wealth have been destroyed."" And Abdullah bin Umar used to perform the Asr prayer while the sun was still shining brightly."
"62","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""The night prayer is offered in pairs of two rak'ahs. When you fear the approach of dawn, then pray one rak'ah as witr."""
"63","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever raises a weapon against us is not one of us."""
"64","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) relieving himself on two bricks while he was facing the Qiblah, and he (Ibn Umar) was on the roof of the house. Ayyub (may Allah have mercy on him) says: It is as if he saw him suddenly (unintentionally)."
"65","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked: O Messenger of Allah! How is the night prayer (to be performed)? He replied: ""Two by two (rak‘ahs); when you fear that dawn is about to break, then pray one rak‘ah as witr, which will make your (previous) prayer odd."""
"66","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have had a ring made and engraved on it 'Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)'. Therefore, no one should have such an inscription engraved on a ring."""
"67","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade meeting the goods (of traders) outside (the markets) until they reach the markets, and he forbade bidding over one another’s goods to increase the price."
"68","Nafi’ (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: I was with Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) while he was in the state of Ihram. He took a sheet, so I put a cap on him. He asked: What is this? I said: It is a cap. He said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (a person in Ihram) from wearing a cap?"
"69","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Grant us blessing in our Makkah, and grant us blessing in our Madinah, and grant us blessing in our Shaam, and grant us blessing in our Yemen, and grant us blessing in our Sa’ (a measure), and grant us blessing in our Mudd (a measure)."" A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! (What about) Iraq and Egypt?"" He replied: ""From there the horn of Satan will emerge, and there are earthquakes and tribulations."""
"70","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be rulers; whoever affirms their lies and assists them in their oppression, he is not from me and I am not from him, and he will not be able to come to me at the Pond of Kawthar. And whoever does not affirm their lies and does not assist them in their oppression, then he is from me and I am from him, and he will come to me at my Pond."""
"71","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he stated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw lice on the face of Ka'b bin Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked: ""Perhaps the lice on your head are troubling you?"" He said, yes. The Prophet said: Shave your head and give fidya (compensation). He (Ka'b) said: I gave a cow as fidya, I braided its necklace and performed ish'ar (ritual marking)."
"72","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he stated: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, when a traveler came and sat down before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, with his knees close to his. Then he asked: What is Islam? He replied: “To bear witness that there is no deity except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, to perform the five prayers, to fast in the month of Ramadan, to pay zakat, and to perform Hajj to the House of Allah.” He asked: If I do all this, am I a Muslim? He replied: “Yes.” He said: You have spoken the truth. He then asked: What is faith (iman)? He replied: “To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, and His messengers, and to believe in the Last Day, resurrection, reckoning, Paradise, Hell, and destiny.” He asked: If I do this, am I a believer? He replied: “Yes.” He said: You have spoken the truth. He then asked: What is excellence (ihsan)? He replied: “To worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then (know that) He surely sees you.” He asked: If I do so, am I a doer of good (muhsin)? He replied: “Yes.” He then asked: When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) come? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the one being questioned knows no more about it than the questioner.” He asked: What are its signs? He replied: “When the barefoot, naked people begin to boast over one another.” He asked: The homeless people? He replied: Yes. Then the traveler left, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Call that man back.” We went outside and saw no one. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, smiled, then said: “That was Jibreel who came to teach you your religion. In this form, he had never come before.”"
"73","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! Of the two things (that I gave you), not even one was in your control. I gave you authority over your share of wealth at the time when I take your soul, so that I may purify you through it, and (the second thing is) My servants performing the funeral prayer over you after your life comes to an end."""
"74","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to observe mourning for anyone who has died for more than three days, except for her husband."""
"75","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was: ""Here I am, O Allah, here I am. There is no partner for You, here I am. All praise and blessings are for You, and the sovereignty is also for You. There is no partner for You."""
"76","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he stated: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The night prayer is in sets of two rak‘ahs. When you fear the approach of dawn, then pray one rak‘ah (witr) so that what you have already prayed becomes odd."
"77","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he stated: The gemstone of the ring of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was towards the palm."
"78","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, had a ring made of gold and wore it for three days, so the noble Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, also had rings made and wore them. He then took it off and had a ring made of silver and had «محمد رسول اللہ» engraved on it. This ring remained with him until he passed away. Then it remained with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, until he passed away. Then it remained with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, until he passed away. Then it remained with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, for six years. Then he gave it to an Ansari man until it fell into the (Arees) well. It was searched for but not found, so Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, had a similar ring made and had «محمد رسول اللہ صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم» engraved on it."
"79","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Two people involved in a transaction have the option (to cancel the sale) as long as they do not separate, unless they both stipulate the condition of choice."
"80","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trimming the moustache and shaving the pubic hair are from the acts of Fitrah (natural disposition)."""
"81","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would perform the sacrifice (of a camel) in Madinah on the day of Eid al-Adha, and when he did not sacrifice a camel, he would slaughter (a sheep or goat)."
"82","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), a man called out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the mosque and asked, ""Which clothes should a Muhrim not wear?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""A Muhrim should not wear a shirt, turban, cap, or trousers, nor should he wear socks unless shoes are not available. If shoes are not available, then he may wear socks, but he should cut them below the ankles. And he should not use any garment that has been touched with saffron or wars (fragrance)."""
"83","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should eat the meat of the sacrifice for more than three days."" When the sun would set on the third day, Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would not eat from his sacrificial meat."
"84","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person in the state of Ihram may kill five animals: the mouse, the biting dog, the kite, the crow, and the scorpion."""
"85","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had to set out on a journey in haste, he would delay the Maghrib prayer and combine Maghrib and Isha. Nafi’ (may Allah have mercy on him) says that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) also did the same while I was with him."
"86","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three men were traveling when rain and lightning from the sky surrounded them, so they took refuge in a cave of a mountain, when a large rock fell over (the mouth of the cave)."" Then he narrated the hadith in detail."
"87","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the killing of women and children on the day of the conquest of Makkah."
"88","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) stated, it is Sunnah to eat food before performing the prayer."
"89","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks alcohol in this world will not be able to drink it in the Hereafter, unless he repents."""
"90","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said regarding the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he used to pray on his mount. In the same way, he would also perform Witr on his mount. Musa bin Uqbah is of the opinion, narrated from Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him), that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) stated that he saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performing Witr on his mount."
"91","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usamah (bin Zaid) is the most beloved to me, except for Fatimah and others."""
"92","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When the people of Paradise will enter Paradise and the people of Hell will enter Hell, then an announcer will stand among them and say: O people of Paradise! There is no more death now. O people of Hell! There is no more death now. Everyone will remain forever in the place where they are."
"93","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any slave who marries without the permission of his master is an adulterer."""
"94","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade making nabidh from dates before they ripen and from fresh dates. He also forbade making nabidh by mixing busr (unripe dates) and dry dates together."
"95","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that it was submitted to the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ""The left side of the mosque has become completely empty."" So the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever populates the left side of the mosque will receive double the reward."""
"96","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he stated: The tongue of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, (said), ""Do you assume, and they assume."""
"97","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the Talbiyah, he said: ""Here I am, O Allah! Here I am, here I am, You have no partner, here I am. All praise and blessings are for You, and the sovereignty is Yours, You have no partner."" Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would add these words to the Talbiyah: ""Here I am, here I am, here I am, and I seek agreement with You, and all kinds of goodness are in Your hands, all desire and action are towards You (for You)."" Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would touch the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner and would say: ""I have never abandoned this touching, whether in crowd or calm, since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) touching both of them."""
